WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
London, December 1952: five days of smog.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:07.650
About 4,000 people were
known to have died,

3
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:09.390
and it could be many more.

4
00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:15.070
In 2013, IARC, the International
Agency for Research on Cancer,

5
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:19.370
classified outdoor air pollution
as carcinogenic to humans.

6
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:25.510
In 2019, 99 per cent of the world's people
lived where WHO air quality guidelines

7
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:27.050
were not met.

8
00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.290
So if a country cleans its air,
can it prevent lung cancer,

9
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:33.690
even in people who have never smoked?

10
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.350
In this mission, you'll trace where a
city's fine particles really come from.

11
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.230
Then you'll judge clean-air action, from
city streets to international treaties.

12
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.490
Your mission: judge how much lung
cancer cleaner air could prevent.
